And then the other part of this that I'm thinking about is the fact that even though Jesus came and healed and fed and proclaimed truth, you know, like we see in the gospels, that didn't stop the religious leaders from rejecting Him. That didn't stop the Pharisees from saying things like, “He casts out demons by the power of Beelzebul.” Even though He was doing miracles, they were still able to reject Him because they had hardened hearts. So I think what that tells me is that just because someone does good works, it doesn’t necessarily mean they’re going to accept Christ. It's not about external actions alone. There needs to be internal transformation. And I guess I'm really struck by how much of a heart issue this is. Like, if your heart isn't open, even the most miraculous signs won't change your mind. But also, the reality is that the enemy is working hard to distract and deceive people today, especially through social media, through entertainment, through false teachings. And so I think we need to be very intentional about guarding our hearts and minds and being grounded in Scripture so that we don't get caught up in those traps. And I think that's why prayer is so important. Because without prayer, we're vulnerable. We're exposed. We're weak. We're easily led astray. So we need to pray constantly, daily, consistently, and not just for ourselves but for others too.

